From ebd3064be2f15da7d5143b9cc46560efb9073f53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:28:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: Retain Madai boot MX until the CPR handoff

The experimental target's separate MX voters still allow an early normal
Pronto request before CPU-domain attachment retains its calibrated floor.
Name the live APC supply for the RPM provider's boot-only validation and
temporary ACTIVE hold. The paired provider releases the hold only after
an acknowledged enabled AO request covers inherited APC. The existing CPU
attach callback rechecks actual APC before that handoff.

This depends on the boot-APC binding/provider and complete CPR bootstrap
and reply-correlated RPM prerequisites. The ordinary board is unchanged.
This adds no sleep policy, leaves the CPR deep-suspend guard in place and
does not qualify firmware, hardware or full global suspend/abort/reentry.

Fixes: 49cb297d9ca6 ("ARM: dts: qcom: Give Madai CPR a separate active-only MX voter")

Codex generated this change and its host qualification. Human review and
DCO certification remain pending. Nothing has been submitted.
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
index 6bb277582..96fc912b7 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8926-lg-madai-cpr.dts
@@ -224,6 +224,8 @@ cpr: power-controller@f9018000 {
 
 &rpm_requests {
 	regulators {
+		qcom,boot-apc-supply = <&pm8226_apc>;
+
 		pm8226_l3_ao: l3-ao {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <750000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1337500>;
